WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.118 --> 00:00:21.076
Ben gazed around, hoping that Winnie had seen Team Black's first victory.

2
00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:27.068
To his surprise, she was hurrying toward him with a worried look.

3
00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:29.761
"Ben! Can I talk to you for a minute?"

4
00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:37.832
Ben gulped. What did she want to talk to him about? His eyes flicked to Zork.

5
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.216
Serena rushed toward him too.

6
00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:44.384
"Actually, we need to talk to you."

7
00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:50.604
She pointed toward a quiet spot under a tree. "Over there."

8
00:00:50.605 --> 00:00:57.420
Ben followed the witches. He was so nervous, he thought he'd explode.

9
00:00:57.421 --> 00:01:00.363
"Winnie, what's up?"

10
00:01:00.364 --> 00:01:03.859
"We think Team Orange may be cheating!"

11
00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:09.412
"Whew!" Ben blew out a sigh of relief. "Is that all?"

12
00:01:09.413 --> 00:01:11.932
Winnie blinked in surprise.

13
00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:17.115
"Did you hear what I said, Ben? We think Team Orange is cheating," she repeated.

14
00:01:17.116 --> 00:01:21.693
"As in, breaking the rules so they can win Field Day."

15
00:01:21.694 --> 00:01:27.479
Serena looked back and forth from Winnie to Ben.

16
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.749
"I think he thought you were going to break up with him, Winnie. Am I right, Ben?"

17
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.798
Blushing, Ben nodded.

18
00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:40.270
"Huh? Why in the world would you think that?" Winnie asked.

19
00:01:40.271 --> 00:01:44.208
"Because you've been talking to Zork for the past two days," Ben said.

20
00:01:44.209 --> 00:01:46.230
"And you've been ignoring me."

21
00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:48.915
Winnie shook her head in confusion.

22
00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:53.749
"We can talk about that later. Right now we have to tell you what Serena heard!"

23
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.635
Serena leaned forward.

24
00:01:56.636 --> 00:02:06.331
"I heard a rumor that Zork made some cuts in the rope with his claw during the tug-of-war."

25
00:02:06.332 --> 00:02:09.770
"That's a huge accusation," Ben said.

26
00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:15.172
"You can't accuse someone of cheating based on a rumor. You need actual proof."

27
00:02:15.173 --> 00:02:19.320
"We have other proof," Serena said.

28
00:02:19.321 --> 00:02:25.369
"Right before Mog's sack ripped, I saw Brunhilda mumbling to herself," Winnie said.

29
00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:29.928
"I'd bet my favorite broomstick that she was casting a spell."

30
00:02:29.929 --> 00:02:35.601
"She was mumbling right before Waldo got itchy too," Serena added.

31
00:02:35.602 --> 00:02:42.641
"And I suspect that she's going to try to use magic in the cross-country race as well."

32
00:02:42.642 --> 00:02:48.717
Ben stared at the two witches. "Even if this stuff is true, what can we do about it?"

33
00:02:48.718 --> 00:02:50.631
"We can talk to Mr. Freaky.

34
00:02:50.632 --> 00:02:54.784
Maybe he can take a closer look at the rope," Winnie said.

35
00:02:54.785 --> 00:03:01.601
"And we can tell some teachers to watch Team Orange during the final race." Serena scowled.

36
00:03:01.602 --> 00:03:05.220
"Ugh! I hate cheaters."

37
00:03:05.221 --> 00:03:09.846
"Some of the cross-country race goes through the woods," Ben said.

38
00:03:09.847 --> 00:03:13.887
"It won't be easy to keep an eye on all the runners at the same time."

39
00:03:13.888 --> 00:03:16.899
Anger flashed in Winnie's green eyes.

40
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.302
"I don't think all the runners have to be watched. Just two of them!"

41
00:03:21.303 --> 00:03:26.923
Ben nodded, and Winnie and Serena hurried off to talk to Mr. Freaky.

42
00:03:26.924 --> 00:03:31.927
Ben returned to his team and told them what the witches had reported.

43
00:03:31.928 --> 00:03:37.609
Waldo shook his head. "I can't believe Zork and Brunhilda would do that."

44
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:44.643
"Yeah," Mog said. "Zork is a really good athlete. Doesn't he want to win fairly?"

45
00:03:44.644 --> 00:03:48.213
"Field Day is supposed to be fun," Jen said.

46
00:03:48.214 --> 00:03:52.185
"It's not supposed to be all about winning."

47
00:03:52.186 --> 00:03:55.151
Ben looked down, feeling embarrassed.

48
00:03:55.152 --> 00:03:59.071
Like Zork, he'd been thinking a lot about winning today too.

49
00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:04.501
He'd wanted to beat Zork. "At least I never considered cheating," he thought.

50
00:04:04.502 --> 00:04:08.140
Mr. Gwarg was getting ready to start the race.

51
00:04:08.141 --> 00:04:12.130
"We'll keep an eye on those two as we run," Mog said.

52
00:04:12.131 --> 00:04:14.419
"But we still have to win, you guys.

53
00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.184
So remember to keep running, no matter what."

54
00:04:18.185 --> 00:04:22.782
"Or keep floating!" Pixel said, grinning at Ben.

55
00:04:22.783 --> 00:04:27.988
Deb had been quiet. "I'd never cheat," she said quietly.

56
00:04:27.989 --> 00:04:31.424
"But I'm going to watch for ways to outsmart them."

57
00:04:31.425 --> 00:04:40.165
Soon Mr. Gwarg was directing the runners to the starting point.

58
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:48.247
The race would go around the school and then into the woods before returning to the school grounds and the finish line.

59
00:04:48.248 --> 00:04:53.172
"Remember to stay on the course," the teacher said.

60
00:04:53.173 --> 00:04:57.638
"Ready . . . set . . . go!"

61
00:04:57.639 --> 00:05:02.411
As Ben zoomed off, he shot a quick look at his teammates.

62
00:05:02.412 --> 00:05:06.112
The best runners on Team Black were Deb and Mog.

63
00:05:06.113 --> 00:05:12.708
Ben could float very fast, but it was going to be a huge challenge for him to beat Team Orange.

64
00:05:12.709 --> 00:05:16.326
Their runners were already off to a strong start.

65
00:05:16.327 --> 00:05:20.722
Scampering on all fours, Lon had shot to a quick lead.

66
00:05:20.723 --> 00:05:24.520
Gaby's long legs were helping to keep her in second place.

67
00:05:24.521 --> 00:05:30.957
Zork and Mog came next, with Ben, Cleo, Carly, and Deb close behind.

68
00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:37.600
That left Pixel, Waldo, Brunhilda, and Jen bringing up the rear.

69
00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:42.744
The runners circled the school, keeping their positions.

70
00:05:42.745 --> 00:05:46.264
So far Ben hadn't seen any signs of cheating.

71
00:05:46.265 --> 00:05:53.897
"But that could change," he thought, especially once they entered the woods.
